															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/recursiverecursion" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1864349); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1864349&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608196106" alt="RecursiveRecursion" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1864349)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/recursiverecursion" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1864349); return false;" >RecursiveRecursion</a></span> <span class="odate time_1512970131 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">11 Dec 2017 05:28</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3649730">
									

<p>Special thanks to Zyn for helping me out in the forums and on #thecritters.<br />
With this, I tried to make a new approach to Extranormal Events, as they're normally sweet and to the point, kind of underutilized as story devices in my opinion. This EE is basically a story that fell short of making it to official SCP status.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">What,&nbsp;you&nbsp;aren't&nbsp;tired&nbsp;of&nbsp;collapsibles&nbsp;yet?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">ok&nbsp;then</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>In case I wasn't clear enough, the anomaly described within is a sort of bug like entity, comparable to a tarantula hawk wasp. It messed with Warren's head by making a series of high frequency sounds, explaining his episodes. When this started to wear off (as it didn't need him anymore), he lost it and tried to smash the eggs. That's right, the rocks are eggs. Tarantula hawks paralyze spiders and plant a single egg in their prey, leaving it as sustenance for when it hatches. Here, the anomaly more or less did the same thing, but with Daniels and the rest of the village it butchered. It went after the team (specifically Daniels) because he took one of the eggs.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

